      "probability": 0.05,
      "rationale": "With multiple tests across lag times and instruments, some correlations near the boundary of significance could be statistical flukes. However: (i) all four autocorrelations are *negative*, not a mix of signs—the consistency argues against chance; (ii) chance levels for best-match lags are provided, and most observed correlations lie beyond ±1σ of those; (iii) I would not normally surface an observation unless it met a reproducibility threshold. Low credence, but cannot be zero.",
